g across all AI agent conversations\n- **Local Storage**: Memory is stored locally on your machine\n- **Multi-Agent Support**: Works with Claude Code, GitHub Copilot CLI, Cursor, and other AI coding agents\n\n### Value Proposition:\nScritty addresses a common problem with AI coding agents: **lack of persistent memory**. Instead of each AI agent \"forgetting\" previous conversations, Scritty creates a shared knowledge base that agents can reference, reducing the need to re-explain context and potentially cutting token costs by retrieving only relevant memories.\n\n### Availability:\n- Listed on [Product Hunt](https://www.producthunt.com/products/scritty)\n- Also featured on [PoweredByAI](https://poweredbyai.app/project/scritty) and other AI tool directories\n- Appears to be a relatively new tool in the AI developer tools space\n\n---\n\n**Note**: I wasn't able to find extensive user reviews or detailed testimonials in this search. The product appears to be newer or in early stages of adoption. For more detailed reviews, pricing, and user quotes, you may want to check directly on the [Product Hunt page](https://www.producthunt.com/products/scritty) or [PoweredByAI review](https://poweredbyai.app/project/scritty).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
